infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Value receiver vs pointer receiver
  desc Small, immutable-ish data by value; identity- or mutex-holding data by pointer
  compares
    - label Value receiver (a Account)
      children
        - label Operates on a copy
          desc Caller's struct is never touched
        - label Lives on the stack
          desc Zero GC pressure, no heap escape
        - label Free of aliasing bugs
          desc Nobody can mutate it under you
        - label Best for small, read-only methods
          desc Copying a big struct costs on every call
    - label Pointer receiver (a *Account)
      children
        - label Operates on the original
          desc Required to mutate the caller
        - label No copy of big payloads
          desc One word, not N fields, per call
        - label Required for sync.Mutex
          desc A copied mutex breaks mutual exclusion
        - label Potential heap escape + data race
          desc *T can escape the frame and be shared
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
